  "result": "Perfect! All 63 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added two functions to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** \u2014 adds or updates a line\n   - If SKU already exists on the invoice, increases its `qty`\n   - If SKU is new, adds it at the end with catalogue data expanded\n   - Validates `qty` is a positive integer (QTY_INVALID)\n   - Validates SKU exists in catalogue (UNKNOWN_SKU)\n   - Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` if invoice status isn't `'draft'`\n   - Never mutates input, returns `ok(newInvoice)`\n\n2. **`removeLine(invoice, sku)`** \u2014 removes a line by SKU\n   - Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` if invoice status isn't `'draft'`\n   - Returns `fail('LINE_NOT_FOUND')` if SKU isn't on the invoice\n   - Returns `fail('NO_LINES')` if it would remove the last line\n   - Never mutates input, returns `ok(newInvoice)`\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`** with two new codes:\n- `NOT_DRAFT` \u2014 only draft invoices can be modified\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND` \u2014 no line with that SKU on the invoice\n\n**Added 17 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Adding new lines and updating existing lines\n- Catalogue data expansion for new SKUs\n- Removing lines at various positions\n- All error conditions for both functions\n- No mutation of original invoices\n- Preservation of other invoice properties (customerId, issueDate, status)\n\nAll 63 tests pass \u2705",
